    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "Hi all,\n\nWe are working on an in-place real-domain FFT (rdFFT) operator that supports BF16 precision for training large models efficiently (e.g., LLaMA2-7B, RoBERTa-large).\n\nOur approach avoids the current view_as_complex limitation by storing outputs in a split real/imag layout. A helper function converts back to standard complex for comparison with torch.fft.rfft. This allows full forward/inverse round-trip tests in BF16 without needing native complex-BF16 support.\n\nRelated PyTorch issue: #171022\n\nThis may interest anyone working with complex-valued operations in BF16, especially for audio, speech, or large model training.",
    "created_at": "2026-01-06T10:12:35Z",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/117844#issuecomment-3714073718",
    "id": 3714073718,
