    "body": "The [`torch.fft.rfft`](https://docs.pytorch.org/docs/stable/generated/torch.fft.rfft.html) function has a complex-valued tensor output, as do all the other FFT-related functions. Since we don't have a `torch.bcomplex32` (or whatever we decide to name it) dtype, this would need to be introduced first before this could work.\n\nI did try the following diff in the hope that the execution could happen in bfloat16, but it runs into an internal cuFFT error:\n\n\n<details><summary>Diff</summary>\n\n```diff\ndiff --git a/aten/src/ATen/native/SpectralOps.cpp b/aten/src/ATen/native/SpectralOps.cpp\nindex 91a0c3ff8cf..defcfda1e13 100644\n--- a/aten/src/ATen/native/SpectralOps.cpp\n+++ b/aten/src/ATen/native/SpectralOps.cpp\n@@ -1,3 +1,4 @@\n+#include \"c10/core/ScalarType.h\"\n #define TORCH_ASSERT_ONLY_METHOD_OPERATORS\n #include <ATen/core/Tensor.h>\n #include <ATen/Config.h>\n@@ -85,7 +86,7 @@ ScalarType promote_type_fft(ScalarType type, bool require_complex, Device device\n     device.is_cuda() || device.is_meta()\n   );\n   if (maybe_support_half) {\n-    TORCH_CHECK(type == kHalf || type == kFloat || type == kDouble, \"Unsupported dtype \", type);\n+    TORCH_CHECK(type == kHalf || type == kFloat || type == kDouble || type == kBFloat16, \"Unsupported dtype \", type);\n   } else {\n     TORCH_CHECK(type == kFloat || type == kDouble, \"Unsupported dtype \", type);\n   }\n@@ -97,6 +98,7 @@ ScalarType promote_type_fft(ScalarType type, bool require_complex, Device device\n   // Promote to complex\n   switch (type) {\n   case kHalf: return kComplexHalf;\n+  case kBFloat16: return kComplexFloat;\n   case kFloat: return kComplexFloat;\n   case kDouble: return kComplexDouble;\n   default: TORCH_INTERNAL_ASSERT(false, \"Unhandled dtype\");\ndiff --git a/aten/src/ATen/native/cuda/CuFFTPlanCache.h b/aten/src/ATen/native/cuda/CuFFTPlanCache.h\nindex 333c21e94f1..44b15e5b9d5 100644\n--- a/aten/src/ATen/native/cuda/CuFFTPlanCache.h\n+++ b/aten/src/ATen/native/cuda/CuFFTPlanCache.h\n@@ -15,6 +15,7 @@\n #include <stdexcept>\n #include <string>\n #include <unordered_map>\n+#include \"library_types.h\"\n \n namespace at::native::detail {\n \n@@ -310,6 +311,11 @@ public:\n       itype = complex_input ? CUDA_C_16F : CUDA_R_16F;\n       otype = complex_output ? CUDA_C_16F : CUDA_R_16F;\n       exec_type = CUDA_C_16F;\n+    }\n+    else if (dtype == ScalarType::BFloat16) {\n+      itype = complex_input ? CUDA_C_32F : CUDA_R_16BF;\n+      otype = complex_output ? CUDA_C_32F : CUDA_R_16BF;\n+      exec_type = CUDA_C_16BF;\n     } else {\n       TORCH_CHECK(false, \"cuFFT doesn't support tensor of type: \", dtype);\n     }\n\n```\n</details> \n\n<details><summary>Output</summary>\n\n```python\n>>> import torch\n>>> x = torch.rand((16, 64, 256), dtype=torch.bfloat16, device='cuda')\n>>> f = torch.fft.rfft(x)  # RuntimeError: Unsupported dtype BFloat16\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<stdin>\", line 1, in <module>\nRuntimeError: cuFFT error: CUFFT_INVALID_TYPE\n```\n</details>",
